hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18105","Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib, from his father, from his grandfather, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you take the belongings of his companion, seriously nor jokingly, and if one of you finds the staff of his companion, let him return it to him."
"18106","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib ibn Yazid, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Let none of you take the belongings of his companion, jokingly or seriously, and if one of you takes the staff of his brother, let him return it to him. Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib who said: Abdullah ibn al-Saib ibn Yazid narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Let none of you take the belongings of his companion, jokingly or seriously, and if one of you takes the staff of his brother, let him return it to him."
"18107","Qutaybah ibn Saeed narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Hashim ibn Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he supplicated and raised his hands, would wipe his face with his hands. Abdullah said: They have differed with Qutaybah in the chain of this hadith, and I think Qutaybah erred in it; they say: from Khallad ibn al-Saib, from his father."
